{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.TypedCrossingsEncoding","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.TypedCrossingsEncoding","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassComputationChain.typed_crossings_encoding_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassComputationChain.typed_crossings_encoding_unique","kind":"theorem","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/TypedCrossingsEncoding.lean#L32-L55","doc":"**Typed-crossings encoding (derived).**\n\nWork in a field `A` (the Hecke algebra image, where the `½` average\nmakes sense), with `σ` the positive crossing and `H_A = q − q⁻¹`\n(here a scalar `h`).  The Skein form of the Hecke quadratic relation\ngives `σ⁻¹ = σ − H_A · 1` (hypothesis `hinv`).  Each typed crossing\n`c·σ + d·1` then has its `(c, d)` pair **forced**:\n\n* `uu = σ` → `(c, d) = (1, 0)`;\n* `dd = σ⁻¹ = σ − H_A·1` → `(c, d) = (1, −H_A)` (forced by `hinv`);\n* `ud = ½(σ + σ⁻¹) = σ − ½H_A·1` → `(c, d) = (1, −H_A/2)`.\n\nThe `ud`-average identity is derived here by `ring` from `hinv`; this\nis the genuine computation underlying gap 3 (the `½` averaging is the\nsole convention, the rest is forced). ","signatureChunk":0}]}